\paragraph{Limitations.}
% Rethinking Demographics for Realistic Fairness.}
Defining demographic attributes is a challenging task and specifically faces simplifications when used for evaluation, as discussed before. In this course, we treated those attributes as discrete states derived from visually distinguishable features. These simplifications highlight ongoing limitations in image and language models. 

% In this work, we defined fair diversity as equity, i.e., equal representation of all attributes across outputs. Alternative fairness definitions are also valid and can be easily integrated into the evaluation, e.g., based on regional, real-world distributions.

We evaluated the generated images using well-established tools like the VLM Llava. Those models suffer from biases themselves and might be prone to errors.

