\subsection{Templates Used for Tool Feedback}
Table \ref{feedback_mapping} shows the mapping between execution results and hint templates: (1) for test cases that are verified as success, we give a [Passed] signal in the judgement area; (2) for test cases that are verified as failed, we give a [Failed] signal in the judgement area; (3) for test cases that are verified as wrong, we give a clear feedback of [Wrong test case] for individual failures, or [No correct test cases generated] if all test cases are invalid; (4) for format error, we will give the feedback of formatting instructions to guide correct generation.

