        We employ a sliding window approach to identify anomalies by evaluating the deviation of current spectral features from established temporal patterns.
        In this illustrative example, HLSAD successfully detects all three artificially introduced anomalies, whereas traditional graph-based analysis fails to identify the final anomaly that manifests in higher-order interactions.
