Details of the experiments using fixed grace periods are in Appendix~\ref{sec:ap:metrics_gp}.


\subsection{Results}
\label{sec:results}
To assess the accuracy of our proposed technique, we ran simulations for each time window and computed the distances between the event logs obtained via the different simulation techniques, and the original ones. Distances were computed using the metrics proposed in~\cite{CHAPELACAMPA2025102447}. Specifically, CFLD and 3GD assess control-flow related distances, AED and RED measure number of events distributions over time, in absolute or relative terms, respectively. CED and CWD evaluate the simulator's ability to accurately replicate events within the circadian dimension (day and hour of the week). CAR quantifies the accuracy of case arrivals, and CTD measures the difference in cycle time distributions, implicitly capturing the accuracy of execution waiting times~\cite{CHAPELACAMPA2025102447}.

