The main contributions of this paper are as follows:
\begin{itemize}
    \item A {\color{black}collaborative FL framework} is proposed to train a RUL prognostic machine learning model with multiple clients (airlines) without sharing any data.  For this,  a decentralized validation procedure is formalized to validate the machine learning models, which is embedded in the FL framework. As data privacy preservation is crucial in such settings, this decentralized validation procedure does not require the clients (airlines) to share any data or labels. Nevertheless, this decentralized validation procedure is generic, and can be employed for other applications of FL. 
    \item Four robust  approaches are developed to aggregate the parameters for the global model. This enables the development of accurate RUL prognostics even when some clients (airlines) have noisy data samples. 
   % We address the case when  some of the clients within the FL framework have noisy data samples, we develop a robust parameter approach that allows the generation of accurate RUL prognostics despite the fact that the data samples are subject to noise.
