\subsection{Custom Benchmarks}
\label{sec:custom-benchmarks}

In the previous set of benchmarks, the number of combination of paths that need to be checked is rather small (at most 48).
Further, because of the sequential nature of the programs being analyzed, the hyperproperties are checked only on the final state of each quantified program.
Thus, these benchmarks are not exploiting the full potential of $\textrm{OHyperLTL}_\mathit{safe}$.
To further demonstrate the effectiveness of our algorithm, both for an increasing number of observation points, and for large numbers of symbolic paths, we designed a second set of benchmarks. For this set of benchmarks, counterexamples exist but require to check relation at multiple observation points, or to check thousands of combinations of paths.
