To highlight important aspects of this set of benchmarks, we briefly discuss the benchmark \texttt{escalating}, which is one of the thirteen instances.
It consists of the two programs \textsc{Escalating} and \textsc{Limit} and a $\forall\exists$ specification that universally quantifies over traces of the first program and existentially quantifies over traces of the second program.
The programs are synchronized at the beginning of their respective loops, i.e., their state is observed whenever they enter a loop iteration.

