\subsection{Our results} The main goal of this paper is to provide affirmative answers to Problems 1.1 and 1.2 asked in Subsection 1.1. In summary, in this paper we show that {\it under the burst error model, both Reed-Solomon and algebraic geometry codes can be (probabilistic uniquely and list) decoded up to the Singleton bound with quasi-linear complexity. } The detailed results are summarized in the following three main theorems.

