\begin{enumerate}
\item $\fC(\lambda P^{(0)}_{\infty},\calP)$ is $\left(1-\cR-\fg/N-\epsilon, O(1/\epsilon)\right)$-burst list-decodable, where $\cR$ is the rate of the code and $\fg$ is the genus of $E$ (note that usually we have $\fg=O(\epsilon N)$ or $\fg=o(N)$, thus the decoding radius achieves the Singleton bound). Furthermore, if both $N$ and $m$ are $O(1)$-smooth, then $\fC(\lambda P^{(0)}_{\infty},\calP)$ can be list  decoded in quasi linear time $O(\frac1{\ep}N\log N)$.
