\[(\br^T_1,\ldots,\br^T_{n_s})=(\bc^T_1+\be^T_1,\dots,\bc^T_{n_s}+\be^T_{n_s}).\]
By Lemma~\ref{lem:easy}, the number of nonzero $\be_j\neq 0$ is at most $\lfloor \fl/m_s\rfloor+2$. 
%Assume $\bc=\ev_{\calP}(f)$ and $f=\sum_{i=0}^{m_s-1}f_i(x_s)\bx^{\bi}$. By Lemma~\ref{thm:convert}, let $\sC\in{\IRS}_m((k-1)P^{(0)}_{\infty},\calP)$ be the converted codeword of $\bc$. Then the $j$-th column $\sC[j]=\ev_{\calP[j]}(f_j(x_s))^T$. 
By performing G-IFFT on each columns of $(\br^T_1,\ldots,\br^T_{n_s})$, $(\bc^T_1,\dots,\bc^T_{n_s})$ and $(\be^T_1,\dots,\be^T_{n_s})$, we obtain matrices $\sR,\sC,\sE\in \F_q^{m_s\times n_s}$ such that
\[\mathsf R=\left(\begin{matrix}
