  \includegraphics[width=1\textwidth]{figures/fig3.pdf}
  \caption{Illustration of $\texttt{Agent} \textsubscript{Scene}$ in VLMLight. Given three-view images from a T-junction (left), a VLM-based Scene Description Agent generates directional-level textual summaries ($T_1$, $T_2$, $T_3$), describing lane semantics, congestion, and special vehicle presence. These summaries are then aggregated into phase-level descriptions ($P$) based on predefined signal phase mappings.}
