\textbf{Capacitated HCP}

In HLP like the $p$-Hub median or the $p$-Hub Location Problem, an additional parameter $p\in \mathbb{N}$ restricts the maximum number of open hubs. These are termed \textbf{capacitated} variants, as opposed to \textbf{uncapacitated} variants, where any number of hubs may be opened. 

Any discussed HCP can be adapted to the capacitated variant by introducing $p\in \mathbb{N}^+$ as an input and adding the constraint:
\[\sum_{h\in H}Y_h\leq p \] 

%It will be shown that no approximation bound for any discussed HCP variant exists, where this additional constraint is included.

